DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       ldapexop issues the LDAP extended operation specified by ooiidd or one  of
       the special keywords wwhhooaammii, ccaanncceell, or rreeffrreesshh.

       Additional  data for the extended operation can be passed to the server
       using _d_a_t_a or base‐64 encoded as _b_6_4_d_a_t_a in the case of ooiidd,  or  using
       the  additional  parameters in the case of the specially named extended
       operations above.

       Please note that ldapexop behaves differently for the same extended op‐
       eration when it was given as an OID or as a specialliy named operation:

       Calling ldapexop with the OID of the wwhhooaammii (RFC 4532) extended  opera‐
       tion

         ldapexop [<options>] 1.3.6.1.4.1.4203.1.11.3

       yields

         # extended operation response
         data:: <base64 encoded response data>

       while calling it with the keyword wwhhooaammii

         ldapexop [<options>] whoami

       results in

         dn:<client’s identity>




